[32m+[m[32m# Student Assistant Chatbot[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA hybrid rule-based + machine learning chatbot that answers common questions from students and incoming enrollees — admissions, tuition, enrollment, and document requests — with support for program-specific and admission-level-specific answers.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBuilt as a thesis project, this chatbot is designed to be reliable without an internet-connected AI service, while remaining architecturally ready to plug in a real LLM later if needed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Features[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Hybrid intent recognition** — combines deterministic rule matching with a trained ML classifier (TF-IDF + Logistic Regression), using confidence thresholds to decide which to trust[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Entity extraction** — recognizes college programs (e.g. "BSCS" → Computer Science) and SHS strands (e.g. "STEM") using spaCy's `PhraseMatcher`[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Context-aware conversations** — remembers what it's waiting to hear (e.g. "which level are you asking about?") across multiple messages, and auto-infers admission level from a mentioned program/strand[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Safety-first design** — critical intents (like ending a conversation) are always handled by deterministic rules, never left to ML or an LLM[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Optional LLM fallback layer** — stubbed and disabled by default; the system works fully without it, and it activates only when rules + ML both fail to understand a message[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Persistent conversation history** — stored in SQLite via SQLAlchemy (users, conversations, messages, feedback)[m
[32m+[m[32m- **REST API** — built with FastAPI, with CORS, rate limiting, input validation, and centralized error handling[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Web chat interface** — plain HTML/CSS/JS frontend, no framework dependencies[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Automated test suite** — 16 tests covering rule matching, ML classification, the API, and edge cases[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Architecture[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mUser (browser)[m
[32m+[m[32m    │[m
[32m+[m[32m    ▼[m
[32m+[m[32mFrontend (docs/index.html)[m
[32m+[m[32m    │  HTTP POST /chat[m
[32m+[m[32m    ▼[m
[32m+[m[32mFastAPI backend (app/api.py)[m
[32m+[m[32m    │[m
[32m+[m[32m    ├─→ ConversationState (per-session memory)[m
[32m+[m[32m    │[m
[32m+[m[32m    ├─→ Hybrid Engine (app/chatbot/engine.py)[m
[32m+[m[32m    │       │[m
[32m+[m[32m    │       ├─→ Rule matching (word-overlap on intents.json patterns)[m
[32m+[m[32m    │       │     — always wins for RULE_ONLY_INTENTS (e.g. goodbye)[m
[32m+[m[32m    │       │[m
[32m+[m[32m    │       ├─→ ML Classifier (app/ml/classifier.py)[m
[32m+[m[32m    │       │     — TF-IDF + Logistic Regression[m
[32m+[m[32m    │       │     — used when confidence ≥ 0.5[m
[32m+[m[32m    │       │[m
[32m+[m[32m    │       ├─→ Entity Extraction (app/chatbot/entities.py)[m
[32m+[m[32m    │       │     — spaCy PhraseMatcher: programs, SHS strands, admission level[m
[32m+[m[32m    │       │[m
[32m+[m[32m    │       └─→ LLM Layer (app/chatbot/llm_layer.py) — STUBBED[m
[32m+[m[32m    │             — only activates if rules + ML both fail[m
[32m+[m[32m    │             — disabled by default (no API key configured)[m
[32m+[m[32m    │[m
[32m+[m[32m    └─→ Database (app/database/models.py) — SQLite via SQLAlchemy[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Design principle:** every layer is replaceable without breaking the others. The CLI and the API both call the same `get_response()` function; rules and ML share `intents.json` as a single source of truth; the LLM layer is fully optional and the chatbot is provably functional without it.[m
[32m+[m
