[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Maintenance[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Adding a new intent[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Add an entry to `app/data/intents.json` with a `tag`, several example `patterns`, and `responses`[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Retrain the model: `python -m app.ml.classifier`[m
[32m+[m[32m3. If the intent is safety-critical, add its tag to `RULE_ONLY_INTENTS` in `app/chatbot/engine.py`[m
[32m+[m[32m4. Test via CLI or `/docs` before deploying[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Adding a new entity category (e.g. campus, semester)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAdd a new key to `ENTITY_DEFINITIONS` in `app/chatbot/entities.py`, following the existing `{canonical_name: [aliases]}` shape — no other code changes needed to detect it.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Retraining the ML model[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRequired whenever `intents.json` patterns change (not required for response-text-only changes):[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m app.ml.classifier[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mThis regenerates `app/ml/model.pkl`, which is gitignored and rebuilt automatically during deployment.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Deployment[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Backend**: deployed on [Render](https://render.com) (free tier)[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Build command: `pip install -r requirements.txt && python -m spacy download en_core_web_sm && python -m app.ml.classifier`[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Start command: `uvicorn app.api:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT`[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Frontend**: deployed on GitHub Pages, served from the `docs/` folder[m
[32m+[m[32m- `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` is set on the backend to the exact frontend origin (no wildcard) in production[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Known limitation:** SQLite on Render's free tier is not guaranteed to persist across redeploys, since the filesystem is ephemeral. Acceptable for a thesis demo; a hosted Postgres database is a natural upgrade path.[m
[32m+[m
